-- EXPECT-ERROR: is ONE tuple argument, so `Bool[p]` over it cannot relate its parts. A callback of 2 arguments is curried: write `a -> a -> Bool[p]`.
-- `Bool[p]` as a callback's result defines `p` from the callback's
-- arguments; a tuple domain `(a, a)` is ONE argument (a tuple), and a
-- callback of two arguments is the curried chain `a -> a -> Bool[p]`
-- (multi-arg design 2026-10-18 §1.1, s2).
mod R19BoolSugarSeveralArgumentCallback do
  fn f(xs : List(a), k : (a, a) -> Bool[p]) : List(a[p]) do xs end
end
